{"additions":1606,"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\n\nPR 2 of 3 for the user guide: replaces the **Configuration Basics** and **Config Recipes** stubs with full chapters, English and Japanese shipped together, and adds a cargo test that loads every fenced `kdl` example in the guide through the real user-config path — a broken example can no longer ship.\n\nPart of #136 (Config Reference and Troubleshooting remain stubs for PR 3).\n\n## Chapters\n\n**Configuration Basics** (`configuration-basics.md`, en + ja)\n\n- The three layers: builtin → user (`--config` / `$VIG_CONFIG` / `~/.config/vig/config.kdl`, macOS included) → repo-local `.vig.kdl` with the trust model (tracked vs. untracked, the y/n/v/Esc dialog, `trust.json` keyed by worktree + content hash, degrade-not-abort, `repo-config` forbidden inside `.vig.kdl`).\n- The `vig config path / dump / themes / trust [--forget]` subcommands.\n- The \"copy the dump, then trim\" workflow — including *why* trimming matters (a full copy freezes future default improvements).\n- Just enough KDL: nodes, string arguments, properties, children blocks, `//` / `/* */` / slashdash `/-`.\n- Merge rules by node class, verified against `merge.rs`: replace-wholesale top-level nodes; per-key merged `app` / `pane … keys` (presets appended, `\"None\"` unbinds); replace-wholesale `layout` / `tabs` / `bind` per page.\n\n**Config Recipes** (`config-recipes.md`, en + ja) — each recipe is a problem + a complete, pasteable config + what changes on screen:\n\n- Appearance: `theme`, `icons \"none\"`, `image-preview \"halfblocks\" / \"none\"`.\n- Keybindings: rebind/add a key, global `app` keys, unbind with `\"None\"`, what `preset \"nav\"` / `\"search\"` expand to and the explicit-beats-preset / presets-are-appended rules.\n- Tabs: trim / reorder with `pages`, keys address pages by name, binding to a disabled page is an error.\n- Layouts: reading a `split` / `place` / `size` tree (annotated default Git layout), widening a pane, leaving a pane unplaced, bringing the Projects list pane back (the commented example in `default.kdl`), and slots — the GitHub detail `when` / `then` as the worked example, plus the single-case `then=` + `triggers` shorthand and a \"make `pr_detail` the default\" variation.\n- `projects-board` pinning, title and number forms.\n- Repo-local `.vig.kdl`: what belongs there vs. the user config, the trust dialog, `repo-config \"off\"`, `vig config trust --forget`.\n- `github-poll-interval`, `procs-refresh-interval`, `procs-history` (limits and the interval × history arithmetic).\n\nBoth introductions (en/ja) now link the new chapters instead of the \"coming in later PRs\" note.\n\n## How examples are verified\n\nNew `#[cfg(test)]` module `src/core/config/guide_examples.rs`:\n\n- Walks `docs/guide/**/src/*.md` (any `src` dir under `docs/guide`, skipping mdBook `book` output), extracts fenced code blocks with a small line-based extractor (itself unit-tested: info strings, line numbers, indented fences, unclosed blocks).\n- Every block whose info string is exactly `kdl` must parse via `parse_user_kdl` and validate via `Config::with_user` — the same functions the real user-config load path uses, including full startup validation (layouts, keys, actions, themes, intervals).\n- Blocks marked `kdl,ignore` (fragments / deliberate-error demonstrations, 4 total) are skipped.\n- A count floor (`>= 30`; currently **46** verified blocks, 23 per language) guards against the extractor silently matching nothing.\n\n`cargo fmt`, `cargo clippy --all-targets -D warnings`, and `cargo test` (344 tests) are green; `mise run docs:build` builds both books cleanly and all in-page anchors were checked against the generated HTML ids.\n\n## Not verified\n\n- The 4 `kdl,ignore` fragments load nothing by design: two deliberate error demonstrations (`theem` typo, `page:docker` binding with docker not in `pages`) — their error messages were checked against the code but are not asserted by the test.\n- Runtime *behavior* claims (what the screen shows after a config change) are verified against `loader.rs` / `merge.rs` / `repo.rs` / `trust.rs` / `default.kdl` by reading, not by TUI integration tests — consistent with PR 1.\n- No demo recordings: text-only PR, no tape changes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01TreGn5Xh4PjDRv9Yo4QU4w\n","changedFiles":8,"comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T09:32:44Z","deletions":11,"headRefName":"docs/guide-config","labels":[],"number":145,"reviewDecision":"","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLearEw","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟡 Changes recommended\n\nThe new guide-example test currently produces confusing parse error locations and is likely to fail in packaged-source builds where `docs/` is excluded, so it needs small adjustments before it’s reliably shippable.\n\n*Once you've addressed the issues Copilot identified, you can request another Copilot review.*\n\n<details>\n<summary>Pull request overview</summary>\n\nThis PR expands the mdBook user guide with complete “Configuration Basics” and “Config Recipes” chapters in both English and Japanese, and adds a Rust test that CI-verifies all fenced `kdl` examples by parsing/validating them through the real user-config load path.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Replaced the stub guide chapters with full content (en/ja), and updated introductions to link them.\n- Added `src/core/config/guide_examples.rs` to extract fenced code blocks from `docs/guide/**/src/*.md` and validate all ` ```kdl ` examples via `parse_user_kdl` + `Config::with_user`.\n- Wired the new test module into `src/core/config/mod.rs` under `#[cfg(test)]`.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>File summaries</summary>\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| src/core/config/mod.rs | Registers the new test-only guide example verifier module. |\r\n| src/core/config/guide_examples.rs | Implements Markdown fenced-block extraction + a test that validates all guide `kdl` examples. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/introduction.md | Updates English introduction to link the new chapters. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/configuration-basics.md | Adds full English “Configuration Basics” chapter content and examples. |\r\n| docs/guide/src/config-recipes.md | Adds full English “Config Recipes” chapter content and examples. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/introduction.md | Updates Japanese introduction to link the new chapters. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/configuration-basics.md | Adds full Japanese “Configuration Basics” chapter content and examples. |\r\n| docs/guide/ja/src/config-recipes.md | Adds full Japanese “Config Recipes” chapter content and examples. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (1)\n\n**src/core/config/guide_examples.rs:105**\n* `origin` is built as `\"<md path>:<line>\"` and then passed into `parse_user_kdl` as the file path. Since `parse_user_kdl` already formats diagnostics as `<path>:<line>:<col>`, this produces confusing duplicated locations like `...:210:3:5` (where `210` is the Markdown line and `3:5` is the KDL snippet location). Pass the real Markdown file path into `parse_user_kdl`, and keep `origin` only for labeling the overall failure / for the `Config::with_user` source.\n```\n            let origin = format!(\"{}:{}\", file.display(), block.line);\n            let result = parse_user_kdl(&block.body, Path::new(&origin))\n                .and_then(|doc| Config::with_user(&doc, PathBuf::from(&origin)));\n            match result {\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 8/8 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 1\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/td72/vig/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T09:39:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"46a499b6bfabfd13337e3e164c29528d709c1776"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLec98Q","author":{"login":"td72"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T09:41:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a793639eba86269d7fb929a823b2c3289b47d358"}},{"id":"PRR_kwDORNPWJs8AAAABLee9JQ","author":{"login":"copilot-pull-request-reviewer"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"### 🟢 Approval recommended\n\nThe changes are well-scoped and the new CI test meaningfully guards documentation correctness; remaining feedback is limited to minor doc output-detail accuracy.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Review details</summary>\n\n### Suppressed comments (2)\n\n**Previously missed (2)** — in code that hasn't changed since the last review.\n\n**docs/guide/ja/src/configuration-basics.md:99**\n* `vig config trust` の出力には決定・日時・worktree パスに加えて内容ハッシュの先頭（表示用の短縮）が含まれます（`src/main.rs:196-203`）。この行は「worktree、決定、日時」のみと書かれていて不完全です。\n```\n| `vig config trust` | 記憶済みの `.vig.kdl` 信頼決定を一覧（worktree、決定、日時）。 |\n```\n**docs/guide/src/configuration-basics.md:97**\n* `vig config trust` output includes a hash prefix in addition to decision/date/path (see `src/main.rs:196-203`). The guide currently claims it lists only worktree/decision/date, which is incomplete and may confuse users comparing output.\n```\n| `vig config trust` | List the remembered `.vig.kdl` trust decisions (worktree, decision, date). |\n```\n\n- **Files reviewed:** 8/8 changed files\n- **Comments generated:** 0 new\n- **Review effort level:** Lite\n</details>","submittedAt":"2026-08-31T09:45:43Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"COMMENTED","commit":{"oid":"a793639eba86269d7fb929a823b2c3289b47d358"}}],"state":"MERGED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:11Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33379384712/job/99448052336","name":"create-tag","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:22Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:43:18Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378962563/job/99446700970","name":"build (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:35Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378962508/job/99446700781","name":"lint","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:06Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:43:05Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378962563/job/99446700553","name":"build (aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-24.04-arm)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:07Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:43:46Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378962563/job/99446700876","name":"build (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:43:46Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378962563/job/99447145646","name":"upload","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:43:46Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Build"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:11Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33379384712/job/99448009875","name":"publish","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:12Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:51Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378962508/job/99446700841","name":"test (x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, ubuntu-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:43:01Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33378962508/job/99446700611","name":"test (aarch64-apple-darwin, macos-latest)","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:42:05Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CI"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:11Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/td72/vig/actions/runs/33379384712/job/99448036576","name":"homebrew","startedAt":"2026-08-31T09:47:18Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Release"}],"title":"📝 User guide: Configuration Basics and Recipes (en/ja), CI-verified examples"}
